#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:86
#: 6d650ddf13324777a3f3285dbc9a588e
msgid "Pull Request Guidelines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:88
#: 5b2df09a92904b688a926cdcc049caba
msgid "A philosophy we would like to strongly encourage is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:90
#: 2964af8fec9047e4a89c7e6da34f0dcb
msgid "Before creating a PR, create an issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:92
#: e5b8e2f203534adaa6b6d5e7c72ae1ef
msgid "The purpose is to separate problem from possible solutions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:94
#: 1ab0e48c17dc4a04ba5ac8a3dcb72519
msgid ""
"**Bug fixes:** If you’re only fixing a small bug, it’s fine to submit a "
"pull request right away but we highly recommend to file an issue "
"detailing what you’re fixing. This is helpful in case we don’t accept "
"that specific fix but want to keep track of the issue. Please keep in "
"mind that the project maintainers reserve the rights to accept or reject "
"incoming PRs, so it is better to separate the issue and the code to fix "
"it from each other. In some cases, project maintainers may request you to"
" create a separate issue from PR before proceeding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:96
#: 6c49411dc07e436fb582a58f42567ae8
msgid ""
"**Refactor:** For small refactors, it can be a standalone PR itself "
"detailing what you are refactoring and why. If there are concerns, "
"project maintainers may request you to create a `#DIP` for the PR before "
"proceeding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:98
#: ff5c9c363139460296f566bba0c034ef
msgid ""
"**Feature/Large changes:** If you intend to change the public API, or "
"make any non-trivial changes to the implementation, we require you to "
"file a new issue as `#DIP` (DingoDB Improvement Proposal). This lets us "
"reach an agreement on your proposal before you put significant effort "
"into it. You are welcome to submit a PR along with the DIP (sometimes "
"necessary for demonstration), but we will not review/merge the code until"
" the DIP is approved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:100
#: 8eda0b9af74a4dbea2ae3164a679d966
msgid ""
"In general, small PRs are always easier to review than large PRs. The "
"best practice is to break your work into smaller independent PRs and "
"refer to the same issue. This will greatly reduce turnaround time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:102
#: aa7f19a5fd5d4c99b118971f60abc954
msgid ""
"If you wish to share your work which is not ready to merge yet, create a "
"[Draft PR](https://github.blog/2019-02-14-introducing-draft-pull-"
"requests/). This will enable maintainers and the CI runner to prioritize "
"mature PR's."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:104
#: 21fbb987f2ba43b6a6bd76650078ec8c
msgid ""
"Finally, never submit a PR that will put master branch in broken state. "
"If the PR is part of multiple PRs to complete a large feature and cannot "
"work on its own, you can create a feature branch and merge all related "
"PRs into the feature branch before creating a PR from feature branch to "
"master."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:106
#: 0f0b88962c134acd916717dccd78b384
msgid "Protocol"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:108
#: c8b78278d91a4301bd6bc2dde8f288ca
msgid "Authoring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:110
#: fdf87c4f4a6442e98e8362c3d21fd4e1
msgid "Fill in all sections of the PR template."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:111
#: 3e1fca87508e4a5699ad33231dca959a
msgid ""
"Title the PR with one of the following semantic prefixes (inspired by "
"[Karma](http://karma-runner.github.io/0.10/dev/git-commit-msg.html])):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:113
#: bc29fdc8691e4d6896ff948f77b9d32d
msgid "`feat` (new feature)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:114
#: 2ebc07c2079e4b089149c8fe28ce0b55
msgid "`fix` (bug fix)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:115
#: 45fa6686acd04982a199cf744f8f171a
msgid "`docs` (changes to the documentation)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:116
#: 98b3eaf789544f9a94bcd66e03e8c67f
msgid ""
"`style` (formatting, missing semi colons, etc; no application logic "
"change)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:117
#: f4395673111745a1848171afd85da9ac
msgid "`refactor` (refactoring code)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:118
#: 2c9ff3b01b914a049791bf02528b9bbd
msgid ""
"`test` (adding missing tests, refactoring tests; no application logic "
"change)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:119
#: e488f94f06e4460e9ba3fd8e916fad7c
msgid "`chore` (updating tasks etc; no application logic change)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:120
#: 7ec3048648a24624b777826337f92e5e
msgid "`perf` (performance-related change)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:121
#: 19bbc5efe2814bca9607a00e91990632
msgid "`build` (build tooling, Docker configuration change)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:122
#: 97965d2eda514b6ca6c95f33acb699dc
msgid "`ci` (test runner, Github Actions workflow changes)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:123
#: aa1fbf4d506d4c85b1b2802b20534118
msgid "`other` (changes that don't correspond to the above -- should be rare!)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:124
#: 6f4577b432214a56bcfc3cd52fc8a2b4
msgid "Examples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:125
#: 2ada071bf36040c3bdbf08250890439c
msgid "`feat: export charts as ZIP files`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:126
#: 12ec85fa44964696877eab28b4836410
msgid "`perf(api): improve API info performance`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:127
#: 4f1d4f3544084383ae1c69005c0ad033
msgid "`fix(chart-api): cached-indicator always shows value is cached`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:129
#: bd9e79d8f98e4646a7deb3d13a962662
msgid ""
"Add prefix `[WIP]` to title if not ready for review (WIP = work-in-"
"progress). We recommend creating a PR with `[WIP]` first and remove it "
"once you have passed CI test and read through your code changes at least "
"once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:130
#: fe3ab17ac303453b90a0d757b8037682
msgid ""
"If you believe your PR contributes a potentially breaking change, put a "
"`!` after the semantic prefix but before the colon in the PR title, like "
"so: `feat!: Added foo functionality to bar`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:131
#: fd1754605c1345cda09ab6d8303d6697
msgid ""
"**Screenshots/GIFs:** Changes to user interface require before/after "
"screenshots, or GIF for interactions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:132
#: cd85a9e007b0436c9f71f59dff0ae0bd
msgid ""
"Recommended capture tools ([Kap](https://getkap.co/), "
"[LICEcap](https://www.cockos.com/licecap/), "
"[Skitch](https://download.cnet.com/Skitch/3000-13455_4-189876.html))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:133
#: 537a83df1284402db8090403e8a26b7d
msgid ""
"If no screenshot is provided, the committers will mark the PR with "
"`need:screenshot` label and will not review until screenshot is provided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:134
#: 2d5342abfe3744788d27a1b13c794865
msgid ""
"**Dependencies:** Be careful about adding new dependency and avoid "
"unnecessary dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:135
#: 348fbab43fdb4f5087c169bb125a4a8c
msgid ""
"**Tests:** The pull request should include tests, either as doctests, "
"unit tests, or both. Make sure to resolve all errors and test failures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:136
#: 6b87ec5a541742849f1681c08c35fbe4
msgid ""
"**Documentation:** If the pull request adds functionality, the docs "
"should be updated as part of the same PR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:137
#: c5040c5a96394b6e920e5e17d2b9f281
msgid ""
"**CI:** Reviewers will not review the code until all CI tests are passed."
" Sometimes there can be flaky tests. You can close and open PR to re-run "
"CI test. Please report if the issue persists. After the CI fix has been "
"deployed to `master`, please rebase your PR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:138
#: 91c4ddd979784e87bae79e36d3c3a52e
msgid "**Code coverage:** Please ensure that code coverage does not decrease."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:139
#: d674d55219544499b9ea03a14dce029f
msgid ""
"Remove `[WIP]` when ready for review. Please note that it may be merged "
"soon after approved so please make sure the PR is ready to merge and do "
"not expect more time for post-approval edits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:140
#: 0a2b323b591c4099bed8ba0fe5734e58
msgid ""
"If the PR was not ready for review and inactive for > 30 days, we will "
"close it due to inactivity. The author is welcome to re-open and update."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:142
#: 946b8ba1a686423b96d4905748b4f23e
msgid "Reviewing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:144
#: 232abacb55764786821eba69c93cfcf9
msgid "Use constructive tone when writing reviews."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:145
#: 6d8c3cb78aaa4eec9dcb9922478cb795
msgid ""
"If there are changes required, state clearly what needs to be done before"
" the PR can be approved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:146
#: 9ee8ef7c6ceb424eaf08fdc73dd7b911
msgid ""
"If you are asked to update your pull request with some changes there's no"
" need to create a new one. Push your changes to the same branch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:147
#: 6824e4f05710469a8e829fe9cebd50b3
msgid ""
"The committers reserve the right to reject any PR and in some cases may "
"request the author to file an issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:149
#: 86994e55592e45cbb0376558dcabff11
msgid "Merging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:151
#: 9ed74f64b9494a589e03fe7e8d4220a7
msgid "At least one approval is required for merging a PR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:152
#: 2ba8da2a0d2a4efda743c01f1ccf2d0a
msgid "PR is usually left open for at least 24 hours before merging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:153
#: 08a5230bceb9487f9fab672990298681
msgid ""
"After the PR is merged, [close the corresponding "
"issue(s)](https://help.github.com/articles/closing-issues-using-"
"keywords/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:155
#: b1efd1fd12894259af1a03fa48715451
msgid "Post-merge Responsibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:157
#: 336d22a88bbf458db5a435f4adb58c15
msgid ""
"Project maintainers may contact the PR author if new issues are "
"introduced by the PR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:158
#: a55a2d58ec6c4bd282f07f4b862692c6
msgid ""
"Project maintainers may revert your changes if a critical issue is found,"
" such as breaking master branch CI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:160
#: cb48a99bb5ae43a8a58243bdb45cce54
msgid "Managing Issues and PRs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:162
#: b4c30ceb9c69462d98cb191e416922f4
msgid ""
"To handle issues and PRs that are coming in, committers read issues/PRs "
"and flag them with labels to categorize and help contributors spot where "
"to take actions, as contributors usually have different expertises."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:164
#: 7992853b054b460f9c0d068414c30130
msgid "Triaging goals"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:166
#: fa77b9634b1c45738c73bdc4955df31a
msgid ""
"**For issues:** Categorize, screen issues, flag required actions from "
"authors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:167
#: 260114156388478991231023ecb9ec6e
msgid ""
"**For PRs:** Categorize, flag required actions from authors. If PR is "
"ready for review, flag required actions from reviewers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:169
#: 57891efe15964a7998da3114dc6a785f
msgid ""
"First, add **Category labels (a.k.a. hash labels)**. Every issue/PR must "
