#: 65936a85e37d42bd8cd7efc697c41917
msgid "Then add other types of labels as appropriate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:183
#: a73f58c1cace4404b47b76c4d8e30f9e
msgid ""
"**Need labels:** These labels have pattern `need:xxx`, which describe the"
" work required to progress, such as `need:rebase`, `need:update`, "
"`need:screenshot`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:184
#: 901055299083483c92c58cbb3d91902c
msgid ""
"**Risk labels:** These labels have pattern `risk:xxx`, which describe the"
" potential risk on adopting the work, such as `risk:db-migration`. The "
"intention was to better understand the impact and create awareness for "
"PRs that need more rigorous testing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:185
#: 5ab19975408544f1b002642e2643ff62
msgid ""
"**Status labels:** These labels describe the status (`abandoned`, "
"`wontfix`, `cant-reproduce`, etc.) Issue/PRs that are rejected or closed "
"without completion should have one or more status labels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:186
#: a7210c9b52e5472b92899f5a79caef69
msgid ""
"**Version labels:** These have the pattern `vx.x` such as `v0.28`. "
"Version labels on issues describe the version the bug was reported on. "
"Version labels on PR describe the first release that will include the PR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:188
#: 1f67faf34e004742aa66d0a89a6ecaa0
msgid ""
"Committers may also update title to reflect the issue/PR content if the "
"author-provided title is not descriptive enough."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:190
#: 899c9c397143465e8191e88e0a54439e
msgid ""
"If the PR passes CI tests and does not have any `need:` labels, it is "
"ready for review, add label `review` and/or `design-review`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/contributing/contributing.md:192
#: dbe095b29ea443aa939355f0ace5babd
msgid ""
"If an issue/PR has been inactive for >=30 days, it will be closed. If it "
"does not have any status label, add `inactive`."
msgstr ""

